    "old_torghut_southern_league": {
      "abolition_note": "Four banners under the Zorigtu Khan (Manchugjab, with Regent Senchin Living Buddha executed by Jin Shuren in April 1932 for resisting gaituguiliu). Sheng Shicai imprisoned Manchugjab in 1937 and enacted formal banner abolition (feimeng gaixian / Hetong County) in 1938-1939; however, Manchugjab was freed in September 1944 and restored as Khan/League Chief by the Nationalist government in 1947 until PRC democratic reform in 1950 (leading to Bayingolin Mongol Autonomous Prefecture in 1954).",
